# Codex's review of slice 304 (FORMAL-DEFAULT-FORMS): a formal whose written default is not a literal of its type is not
# built by this translation (lm_compiler_formal_default_kind 2); read as a merge operand, the args part holds no value for
# it -- no zero stands in, and the reading of f\args evaluates no default (the author: a computed default is evaluated by
# each call omitting the formal).  With no later operand writing the field the part is refused at the operand: the limit of
# this phase, not a rule of the language.  Filled later (merge(comp\args; (int: a 5))) it runs in merge_args_operand.
fn: comp (int: c 3; int: a 2 + 3) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: comp
fn: m () int
    pack: merge(comp\args)
    return: pack\c
end: m
send: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
